From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ash: NickelOS local accounts

NickelOS has no Google sign-in. An account is created on the device: a
real Linux user (nickel-accountsd) with an encrypted home protected by
its password, and no Google account.

Identity: a regular user whose AccountId email is
"<username>@nickel.localhost" (session_manager needs an email-like id);
user_manager::IsNickelLocalAccount() recognizes it by that domain
(components/user_manager/nickel_local_account.h).

Creating an account: the new LocalAccountCreationScreen (name,
username, password; WebUI local-account-creation) replaces the user
creation, Gaia info and Gaia screens in setup and "Add person". It asks
nickel-accountsd (org.nickelos.Accounts) for the Linux user, the first
account being the owner and an administrator, then signs in as a new
regular user. AuthSessionAuthenticator adds the chosen password as the
account's "local-password" factor when it creates the encrypted home.
If signing in fails the Linux user is removed again.

Signing in: the login screen always offers the offline password for
local accounts; they are never sent to online sign-in or recovery. The
display name comes from the Linux user's GECOS field.

Places that assume every regular user has a Google account skip local
accounts: IsLoggedInAsUserWithGaiaAccount(), token handles, the auth
error observer, sync consent migration, user cloud policy, the locale
switch, sync consent and recovery screens, the Gaia profile image and
Google Photos wallpapers. SaveUserType() no longer requires an account
id key (local accounts have none).

